# Repository root.
#
# `api/` and `web/` carry their own .gitignore for vendor, node_modules and
# their .env files. This one covers what lives beside them, and the reason it
# exists is that nothing here was ignored at all - a `git add -A` was one
# keystroke away from publishing a production APP_KEY.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
#
# deploy/.env.production holds the live APP_KEY, the database password and the
# fingerprint reader's push token. A repository is the wrong place for any of
# them: it is copied to every clone and every fork, and a key is still a key
# after it has been deleted from the tip of the branch.
#
# Keep the file on your own machine and upload it to the host by hand.
/deploy/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ------------------------------------------------------------- build output
#
# Release archives are 13 MB each and are rebuilt from source by
# build-release.ps1, so a repository full of them is cost without benefit.
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- local junk
debug.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
